        ":question/worked-solution": "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}\u2061A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\u2220A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=10\\text{\u00a0cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m\u2220A & ={120}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{120}^{\u2218}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 10\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061{120}^{\u2218} \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 10\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =5b\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 25\\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} & =5b\\cdot \\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} \\\\ 5b & =25 \\\\ b & =5\\text{\u00a0cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=5\\,\\text{\u00a0cm}.$",
