        "title": "Calculating an Angle or Side of a Triangle Given the Area of a Triangle"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "55d7cd50-6834-55b6-a52f-4f6d251b49dd",
        ":question/problem": "![](images/85/85b13f2236c5f00da34ea71fdbfc967882fa6e66c347f6ef40c0604391a5d68e.png)\n\nThe area of \u200b\u200bthe triangle $\u25b3ABC$ is $15{\\text{\u00a0cm}}^{2}.$ Find $m\u2220A.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}\u2061A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\u2220A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5\\,\\text{\u00a0cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=12\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m\u2220A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\ 15 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\ 15 & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\ \\frac{15}{30} & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061A & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ m\u2220A & ={30}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
